  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>&#946;</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#947;</mi></math> be three positive real numbers. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>R</mi></math> be such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math> for all <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8712;</mo><mi>R</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></math> be in arithmetic progression with mean zero, then the value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mi>f</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></math> is equal to</p><p>Given,</p><p>Mean is zero, so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow><mi>n</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>Now this means that&nbsp;first and last term, second and second last and so on are equal in magnitude but opposite in sign.</p><p>Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p><p>Now finding&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mi>f</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mfenced><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>5</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mfenced><mrow><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi><mn>3</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>&#947;</mi><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mi>&#947;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;......equation<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;{as first &amp; last, second and second last and so on are equal in magnitude and opposite in sign}</p><p>Now given&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math></p><p>So,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced close=\"]\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mi>f</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>n</mi></mfrac><munderover><mo>&#8721;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mi>f</mi><mfenced><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;{from equation<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math> }</p></blockquote>"
